course: dictionary
lesson: 8926
title: Sight: seeing and the sights
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sight is a word with more than one meaning, and the clues around it tell you which one. As a noun, sight is the ability to see. «Children who leave the path and lose sight of their group get lost quickly» means they can no longer see their group.
explain: A sight is a thing you see, especially something special or interesting. «Tourists see the sights of a city» means they visit interesting places and look at interesting things. Here sights is plural, so there are many things to look at.
explain: Phrases give strong clues. «In sight» means able to be seen, and «out of sight» means not able to be seen. «A live third rail or an overhead wire can kill without any train in sight» means the danger is real even when no train can be seen.
explain: Sight can also be a feeling about a welcome thing. «A sight for sore eyes» means something you are happy to see after a long time. To check any meaning, swap in a simpler word, such as «seeing» or «view», and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Sight means the ability to see, and it is one of the five senses.
fact: The other four senses are hearing, touch, taste and smell.
fact: A sight is something you see, especially something special or interesting.
fact: «In sight» means able to be seen, and «out of sight» means not able to be seen.
fact: To sight something means to see it, especially something rare or far away.
exercise: «Children who leave the path and lose sight of their group get lost quickly.» What does lose sight of mean here? | Feel sad about them | Hold their hands tightly | *Cannot see them any more | Count them every hour
exercise: In science, what is sight? | The name of a planet | *One of the five senses, the ability to see | A kind of loud noise | A type of rock
exercise: «Tourists see the sights of a city.» What are the sights? | *Interesting places and things to look at | Lost children | Bags of food | Dark, empty streets
test: «Keep in sight of your adult at busy places.» What does in sight mean? | Holding a ball | Hurrying quickly | *Able to be seen | Very far away and hidden
test: «Light from very distant stars has not had time to reach us, so in most directions our sight runs out into darkness.» What does sight mean here? | *The view our eyes can reach | A kind of star | A loud, bright noise | A shop window
exam: «Out of sight, out of mind» means what? | Things you lose are always found | Rain falls quickly from the sky | *You forget things you cannot see | You see things far away more clearly
